{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhbV7p3MKQGKq45ZEqxj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YU8sxdStwKkP7CpsBqRpXM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4\ncat << 'EOF' > $D/hypothesis.md\nRefinement of the incumbent `iter0_candidate3` (Kahneman & Tversky local representativeness with person-specific decision sensitivity): people judge randomness by the same multiscale local balance plus irregularity score, but their sense of \"periodic pattern\" only picks up repeating templates longer than two flips (e.g. HHT-HHT, HHTT-HHTT); streaks (period 1) and plain alternation (period 2) are judged only through the balance and alternation-rate cues, not penalised a second time as periodic patterns. The single change is this non-redundant periodicity penalty, addressing the critique that the incumbent over-penalises perfect alternation (and, more weakly, long streaks) relative to what people choose.\nEOF\necho nonredundant_periodicity_representativeness > $D/model_name.txt\nsed -e 's/^    for period in range(1, (n \\/\\/ 2) + 1):/    for period in range(MIN_PERIOD, (n \\/\\/ 2) + 1):/' \\\n    -e 's/^LOCAL_WINDOW = 4$/LOCAL_WINDOW = 4\\nMIN_PERIOD = 3  # periods 1 (streaks) and 2 (alternation) are not periodic templates/' \\\n    /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/models/iter0_candidate3.py > $D/candidate.py\npython3 - << 'EOF'\np=\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/iter_1/candidate_4/candidate.py\"\ns=open(p).read()\ni=s.index('\"\"\"',3)+3\ndoc='''\"\"\"Refinement of iter0_candidate3: non-redundant periodicity penalty.\n\nPeople judge randomness by the Kahneman & Tversky local-representativeness\nscore (multiscale local balance plus irregularity relative to an\nover-alternating prototype and periodic templates), with a person-specific\ndecision sensitivity. The single change: the periodic-template penalty only\nconsiders templates of period >= 3, so streaks (period 1) and perfect\nalternation (period 2) are judged only through the balance and alternation\ncues instead of being penalised twice.\n\"\"\"'''\ns=doc+s[i:]\ns=s.replace(\"# `tests/test_raw_features_seeds.py` pins\",\"# (periodicity_score is modified here: MIN_PERIOD.) `tests/test_raw_features_seeds.py` pins\")\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"MIN_PERIOD\\|period in\" $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment1/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2923,"cache_read_input_tokens":51145,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2923,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c2a329c-f0b5-4f32-bd80-8e37fff88b8f","uuid":"d835295e-a423-49b0-b43f-ebe5dad43921","timestamp":"2026-10-04T17:31:42.974Z","request_id":"req_011CfhbV7QUbr6bq68h353m3"}
